A||||7||2M4 Dale||Powerstat = Horsepower ??? How ?||||5||
Z||000000||2M4 Dale||05-26-2000||09:44 AM||||How can a thermostat increase horsepower ? More flow...so less resistance on water pump ? More flow so cooler opperating temps ?<P>I read somewhere that the addition of a low temp powerstat enhances power output.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-26-2000||09:49 AM||||Cooler water = more hp.  Just like a dam.  The wind cools the water that flows through the dam which in turn produces more electricity.  This is why there's more technology in N. America as opposed to S. America.  It's warmer down there, so the water produces less power and is able to power less computers, etc.<P>(Are you buying any of this? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Didn't think so.  Have you guessed that I don't have the slightest clue? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-26-2000||10:35 AM||||It does some fooling to the cars computer so it gets more air and fuel. works best if your car has a turbocharger because it generates a lot more heat. My 2.8 has an Airresearch turbo and I run a 160* temp stat and 175* fan control switch. No top end performance at all with the OEM 195*||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||05-26-2000||11:18 AM||||Well I went ahead and put one in my Iron Duck. What the hay...if I get 1 horse more that will be an improvement I guess...lol Next is a K&N air filter and oil filter and some fresh Castrol.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phaeton||05-26-2000||09:54 PM||||The ECM puts more advance on a colder engine.  When the engine gets hot the computer worries overmuch about detonation and backs the timing off.||||reg||12
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||05-27-2000||12:01 AM||||I was gonna say that, but terryk beat me to it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||2M4 Dale||05-27-2000||12:16 AM||||Well the Duck runs pretty darn good. Not sure how much the stat helped but maybe I noticed a little something. Probably just my imagination...lol ||||reg||6
Z||000008||Ozzy||05-27-2000||12:42 AM||||Yeah right on SCCA...I sure wish that terryk would study his darn facts a little more! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Hey 2m4 Dale... I dont care whut they say, I had done about everything you can to my '88 DIS "iron puke" (SCCA patent pending! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) in the line of stock new components... sensors, new IAC, rebuilt the 700 TB, replaced intake man. gasket, plugs, wires, yada, yada, yada!<P>It made it run and idle better but then I thought I'd try the 165 deg. thermostat and K&N air filter. ASS-O-METER or not, the performance improvement was VERY noticable. Before it would rev to 5k but with next to no pull over about 3700 rpm. After the stat and filter, it actually still develops a little power right up to 5500 rpm. I dont push it that hard regular like 'cause I can almost hear that crank bending but it does do it. To re-enforce the extra fuel theory, I recently did a road trip and got 34 m.p.g. I remember checking my mileage on the same run before I added the stat and filter and it was closer to 36 mpg. <P>Ozzy||||reg||10
